==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
Variant of {{m|en|Page}}, from {{m|en|[[page#Noun_2|page]]||}}, from {{der|en|fro|page}}, possibly via {{der|en|roa-oit|paggio}}, from {{der|en|la-lat|pagius||servant}}, probably from {{der|en|grc|παιδίον||boy, lad}}, from {{m|grc|παῖς||child}}; some sources consider this unlikely and suggest instead {{der|en|la|pagus||countryside}}, in sense of "boy from the rural regions".

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/peɪd͡ʒ/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Paige.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪdʒ|s=1}}
* {{homophone|en|page}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|~|s}}

# {{surname|en|southern [[English]]|from=occupations}}, a variant of [[Page]].
